# Citation metadata for AstroTwo (Citation File Format 1.2.0, https://citation-file-format.github.io/).
# Kept in step with src/astrotwo/__init__.py (version) by tests/test_citation_cff.py.
# .zenodo.json repeats title, author, licence, keywords, abstract and repository: kept in step by
# tests/test_zenodo_json.py.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AstroTwo in your research, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "AstroTwo"
abstract: >-
  AstroTwo is a macOS application for astrophysicists: a HiPS sky atlas with FITS images,
  catalogues, Virtual Observatory queries (cone search, ADQL), cross-match and sourced
  object profiles. It works alongside Aladin, TOPCAT and DS9 through SAMP. An optional
  AI assistant runs AstroTwo commands and never produces numbers by itself.
authors:
  - given-names: "Guido"
    family-names: "Ratti"
    # ORCID: not available yet. Add it here when it exists, e.g.
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-13"
license: "GPL-3.0-or-later"
repository-code: "https://github.com/guidogg13/AstroTwo"
# DOI: to be added after the first archive on Zenodo, e.g.
# doi: "10.5281/zenodo.0000000"
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - astrophysics
  - sky atlas
  - HiPS
  - Virtual Observatory
  - SAMP
  - macOS
